    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d551-a2">

                <pb facs="0679" n="365" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg365"/>


                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grey</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the American
                        Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office</hi>, <lb/>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 28, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs presents his compliments to the United
                    States Ambassador and has the honour to inform his excellency, with reference to
                    an enquiry dated the 18th instant addressed by the United States Consul General
                    to the board of trade on the subject of the detention of the steamships <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Fridland</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Björnstjerne
                        Björnson</hi>, that these vessels and their cargoes have been put into the
                    prize court where every facility will be given to owners of the cargo to
                    establish their rights.</p>
                <p>The United States Embassy will be duly advised of the finding of the court.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
